 "credits": 2,
 "standfirst": "A full front-end + back-end application built to a real specification, delivered as the MAD II capstone.",
 "instructor": "Prof. Nitin Chandrachoodan &amp; Mr. Thejesh GN",
 "term": "Every term",
 "prereq": "CS2006",
 "syllabus_body_html": "<p>This project is an advanced course that builds on the foundations of \"Modern Application Development - I,\" focusing on creating dynamic web applications using Vue.js. It covers key concepts such as token-based authentication, asynchronous task execution with Celery and Redis, caching techniques, and essential security practices including CORS, enabling students to develop scalable and secure applications.</p>\n      <p><b>Co-requisite:</b> BSCS2003:  Modern Application Development I</p>\n      <p><b>Faculty:</b></p>\n      <ul class=\"link-list\">\n          <li>Prof. Nitin Chandrachoodan, Department of Electrical Engineering, IIT Madras</li><li>Mr. Thejesh GN, Independent Technologist, Multiple Affiliations</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p><b>How the project runs:</b></p>\n      <ul class=\"link-list\">\n          <li>The objective of this project is to provide hands-on experience in developing a web application using Vue.js and related technologies.</li><li>Students build a functional web application featuring interactive front-end components, state management with Vuex, token-based authentication, and asynchronous task execution using Celery and Redis.</li><li>The project reinforces concepts from \"Modern Application Development - I\" and introduces advanced web development techniques.</li><li>The viva consists of two levels, with the final round conducted by industry experts and contributing significantly to the final grade.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p><a href=\"https://study.iitm.ac.in/ds/course_pages/BSCS2006P.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Official syllabus on the IITM study portal →</a></p>\n    <ul class=\"link-list\" style=\"margin-top:14px\"><li><a href=\"https://thejeshgn.com/projects/modern-application-development-2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Screencasts by Thejesh GN</a></li></ul>",
